sing.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm applying the P-FDT setup: two copies of the same algorithm, each seeing a different observation, with the policy mapping observation to action. Working through the payoffs, mutual passing gives each 2, mutual submitting gives each 4, and submitting while the other passes gives me 0 and them 5. I'm pausing on whether utility is measured in years.\n\nI'm checking the (submit, pass) outcome against a prior where I don't yet know which prisoner I am, which makes its expected value 2.5 versus 2 for mutual passing and 4 for mutual submitting. Since both copies run the same algorithm, that symmetry points toward passing.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9203,"completion_tokens":630,"total_tokens":9833,"cost":0.049412,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.049412,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.036812,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.0126},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":453,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}